00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:55.680
Open AI also audited SWE Bench Pro

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.360
and found 30% of its tasks broken.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:01.580
The company is retracting its earlier recommendation

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:03.440
that researchers treat the benchmark

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:06.620
as a reliable measure of frontier coding ability.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:10.340
As Models improve, the audit shows that evals

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:12.420
need to grow harder and more trustworthy

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:14.200
to track genuine progress.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:17.360
Builders working on agentic coding tools

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:20.200
should expect new benchmarks to appear in coming months.

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:23.780
The retraction affects how teams measure tool calling

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:26.540
and long horizon code agents going forward.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.400
It continues the frontier models tracking

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:33.080
from last episode by shifting attention from capability gains

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:34.620
to measurement reliability.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:36.840
Now for the model updates,

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:42.600
and Vidya released Nemotron Labs 3 Puzzle, 75B A9B,

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:45.460
a compressed hybrid mixture of experts model.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:49.940
It reduces parameters from 120.7 billion total

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:55.100
and 12.8 billion active down to 75.3 billion total

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:57.340
and 9.3 billion active.

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:00.680
On a single eight times B200 node,

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:04.860
the model delivers 2.03 times the original throughput

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:07.580
at 100 tokens per second per user.

00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:12.340
On 1H100, it raises 1 million token concurrency

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:13.840
from one request to eight.

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:16.820
The model was built through iterative hardware

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:18.460
where a wear structural compression

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:21.400
followed by short knowledge distillation recovery.

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:25.640
This update advances the AI compute and inference arc

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:28.500
by showing concrete throughput gains from compression

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:31.140
that keeps user experience speed intact.

